# net481 test execution (agent sessions)

Test projects under `Source/Tst/` target `net10.0`, `net8.0`, and `net481` and use **xUnit v3 executables** (`OutputType=Exe`).

In Cursor agent terminal sessions, `dotnet test` for **net481** often hangs during VSTest protocol negotiation (`Failed to negotiate protocol, waiting for response timed out`). The same tests run fine in Visual Studio/ReSharper and via the built xUnit in-process runner. **Treat VSTest timeouts on net481 as an environment limitation, not a product failure.**

## How to run tests

### Modern TFMs (`net8.0`, `net10.0`)

Use `dotnet test` scoped to **one** TFM at a time (serial with other builds/tests in this workspace):

```powershell
dotnet build Source/Tst/<Project>/<Project>.csproj -c Debug
dotnet test Source/Tst/<Project>/<Project>.csproj -c Debug -f net8.0 --no-build
```

Prefer `-f net8.0` (or `-f net10.0`) instead of unscoped `dotnet test`, which launches all TFMs and makes net481 hangs harder to diagnose.

### net481 — run the xUnit v3 `.exe` directly

After a successful build, invoke the in-process runner; do **not** use `dotnet test` for net481 in agent sessions.

```powershell
& "artifacts/bin/<Project>/debug_net481/<Project>.exe" -class "<FullyQualifiedTestClass>" -noColor
```

Examples:

```powershell
# All tests in a class
& "artifacts/bin/KZDev.PrimeTime.Testing.UnitTests/debug_net481/KZDev.PrimeTime.Testing.UnitTests.exe" `
  -class "KZDev.PrimeTime.Testing.UnitTests.UsingThrowHelper" -noColor

# Single method (wildcard supported)
& "artifacts/bin/KZDev.PrimeTime.Testing.UnitTests/debug_net481/KZDev.PrimeTime.Testing.UnitTests.exe" `
  -method "*UsingThrowHelper.ThrowInvalidOperation_RunnerStopJoinTimedOut*" -noColor
```

Use `release_net481` instead of `debug_net481` when validating Release builds.

## Agent discipline

- **Build before test** after any code change; pass `--no-build` only when binaries are already current.
- **Do not retry** net481 `dotnet test` with escalating `VSTEST_CONNECTION_TIMEOUT` — switch to the `.exe` runner.
- **One build or test run at a time** (see `build-and-test-serialization` rule).
- When reporting results, state which runner was used per TFM (e.g. `dotnet test -f net8.0` + exe for net481).
- CI on Linux does not exercise net481; local exe-runner or IDE validation is the complement for that TFM.
